 "summary": "Not on these pairs. On BTC, ETH and SOL, RSI(7) crossing MFI(14) did the same as random entries on 1h, 4h and daily, up or down, with or without the 40 and 60 zones. The one pooled result outside the luck band is fragile: on daily, price after RSI(7) crossed down MFI(14) with both above 60 did 6% worse than random for a short, and almost all of that came from signals between Aug 1 and Sep 9, 2021.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Going long on the cross up",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily. Twenty candles after RSI(7) crossed up MFI(14), price stood where it did after random candles."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting the cross down",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily. The cross down did not mark falls any more often than a random candle did."
  },
  {
   "use": "Cross up with both lines below 40",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily. On 4h in downtrends it looked worse than random, but only because of signals on Nov 8–13, 2022."
  },
  {
   "use": "Cross down with both lines above 60",
   "verdict": "fragile-worse",
   "text": "Worse than random on daily for a short, but only because of signals between Aug 1 and Sep 9, 2021. On 1h and 4h it was the same as random."
  },
  {
   "use": "RSI(7) held above MFI(14)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h and 4h. On daily it formed too few separate moves to judge."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, RSI(7) crossing up MFI(14) gave 16,786 entries in 1,405 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0.01% behind random entries, inside a luck band of 0.04% either way. The cross fires about four times as often on 1h as on 4h, and the mirror cross down lands in the same place. Requiring both lines below 40 leaves about a quarter of the 1h entries and changes nothing.",
  "The only pooled result outside the band is the daily short after RSI(7) crossed down MFI(14) with both lines above 60. Price did 6% worse than random for the short after 20 days, and SOL alone did 12% worse. Both rest on 7 signals between Aug 1 and Sep 9, 2021, and without them the result is the same as random. It shows at 10 candles but not at 50 or 100, and neither the uptrend nor the downtrend half falls outside its band on its own.",
  "The regime split changes one reading. On 4h, the cross up with both lines below 40 was the same as random in uptrends. In downtrends it did 0.61% worse than random, but that rests on 5 signals on Nov 8–13, 2022, during the FTX collapse. On daily the same setting formed too few separate moves to judge in uptrends and was the same as random in downtrends.",
  "Single stretches also produce the per-coin results. On 1h, RSI(7) held above MFI(14) on SOL beat random by 0.1%, but only because of 760 entries between Feb 4 and Apr 3, 2021. On BTC 1h, the short on a cross down with both above 60 looked worse than random only because of signals on Feb 4–5, 2022. On SOL 4h, the cross up looked worse only because of 45 entries between Apr 25 and Jun 18, 2022.",
  "For a long DCA bot, timing the start on this cross gives the same entries as starting at random, so the DCA orders and take profit decide the result. On 1h the cross fires so often that, as a filter beside other conditions, it removes few entries. The zone versions need two bot conditions, the cross plus a level, and they still matched random. If you short on the daily cross down from above 60, one strong rally can hold the deal against you for weeks, so cap the deal with your stop loss."
 ],
